  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "For this question, use the identity $\\tan 2\\theta=\\dfrac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $t=\\tan15^\\circ$. Show that $\\dfrac{2t}{1-t^2}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt3}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Substituting $\\theta=15^\\circ$ gives $\\tan30^\\circ=\\dfrac{2t}{1-t^2}=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt3}$.",
          "worked": "Let $\\theta=15^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan30^\\circ&=\\frac{2\\tan15^\\circ}{1-\\tan^2 15^\\circ}\\\\\\tan30^\\circ&=\\frac{2t}{1-t^2}\\\\\\frac{2t}{1-t^2}&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $t^2+2\\sqrt3t-1=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Cross multiplying gives $2\\sqrt3t=1-t^2$, so $t^2+2\\sqrt3t-1=0$.",
          "worked": "Cross multiply the equation in part a.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sqrt3t&=1-t^2\\\\t^2+2\\sqrt3t-1&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence show that $\\tan15^\\circ=2-\\sqrt3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The quadratic formula gives $t=-\\sqrt3\\pm2$. Since $\\tan15^\\circ>0$, $\\tan15^\\circ=2-\\sqrt3$.",
          "worked": "Use the quadratic formula.\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=\\frac{-2\\sqrt3\\pm\\sqrt{12+4}}2\\\\t&=-\\sqrt3\\pm2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\tan15^\\circ>0$, reject $-\\sqrt3-2$.\n$$\\tan15^\\circ=2-\\sqrt3.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Use a similar technique to find the exact value for $\\tan22.5^\\circ$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan22.5^\\circ=\\sqrt2-1$. Let $u=\\tan22.5^\\circ$; the identity gives $u^2+2u-1=0$. Choose the positive root.",
          "worked": "Let $u=\\tan22.5^\\circ$ and substitute $\\theta=22.5^\\circ$ into the identity.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan45^\\circ&=\\frac{2u}{1-u^2}\\\\1&=\\frac{2u}{1-u^2}\\\\1-u^2&=2u\\\\u^2+2u-1&=0\\\\u&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{4+4}}2\\\\u&=-1\\pm\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\tan22.5^\\circ>0$, reject $-1-\\sqrt2$.\n$$\\tan22.5^\\circ=\\sqrt2-1.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
